title: Renaissance — Loid past-tense governance (settlement-debt T-012 + claimant-accuracy T-013)
summary: 'Implemented Loid''s two settlement-domain protocols. T-012: the captain board now flags settlement-debt (runs whose children are all terminal but the epic never settled — a closed-loop blindspot), detect-only, Cid owns the fix. T-013: settlement re-attributes learning to the dominant child archetype when the parent is a generic ''orchestrator'' claimant, so journal/work-log promotion credits the agent that actually did the work, not a generic bucket. Both preserve the one-way settlement arrow (settledAt only, never status). MCP 453 / CLI 441 green.'
